---
// Lesson 11.2a — Create PT: Video + PPR
// hybrid CPT: record the video, write the final Personalized Project Reference.
import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';

const body = `<h1>11.2a — Create PT: Video + PPR</h1>

<p class="lesson-lead">
    Production day. Two artifacts leave this room as part of your
    AP score: the video (behavior, demonstrated by you, under 60
    seconds) and the Personalized Project Reference — the PPR —
    the ONLY notes you may hold while answering WR2 on exam day.
    Both are made today.
</p>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity hybrid">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Record</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~25 min</span>
    </div>

    <p><strong>Video rules (read twice, then rehearse once
    more):</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>Under 60 continuous seconds, one take (edits are
            forbidden — one unbroken recording)</li>
        <li>Must show: input happening, program behavior, output
            — your <a href="11.1d.html">11.1d</a> demo path</li>
        <li>Voiceover or on-screen text explaining purpose; your
            face is optional, your program is not</li>
        <li>No names of classmates or school (privacy rule)</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Recording ritual:</strong> stopwatch rehearsal →
    recording one → watch it → one fix if needed → recording two,
    done. Retaking forever is a trap; your demo path is already
    rehearsed. Save as MP4 and back it up in TWO places (repo
    folder + cloud).</p>

    <p><strong>The PPR (the exam-day cheat sheet you write
    yourself):</strong> a PDF of up to 5 program components:</p>
    <ol>
        <li>Your list declaration (the real line)</li>
        <li>The procedure with parameters (the real signature)</li>
        <li>The algorithm body (the real code with your three
            S/S/I parts visible)</li>
        <li>A call site (the real call)</li>
        <li>One more: the input handler or the output line</li>
    </ol>
    <p>That PPR prints with you into the exam room on May 14 —
    WR2a/2b/2c are answered FROM IT. Screenshot the exact lines,
    not from memory.</p>

    <div class="bug-hunt">
        <h3>Bug Hunt: Submission-blockers</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Your video shows the Unity editor with your
                school's name in the window title. What does the
                privacy rule say — and what is the 5-second fix
                (crop / rename)?</li>
            <li>The video is 61 seconds. What gets cut — and why
                is it ALWAYS the waiting between inputs, never
                the input or the output?</li>
            <li>Your PPR has "cleaned-up" code that differs from
                the video's behavior. Why must PPR and video
                MATCH exactly (the grader cross-references
                them)?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity hybrid">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Close of Day</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~5 min</span>
    </div>

    <div class="tinker">
        <h3>Tinker: Deliverables</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Both files exist, named and backed up:
                video.mp4 + PPR.pdf in the repo folder.</li>
            <li>Commit + push: <code>"11.2a: video + PPR"</code>.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="checklist">
        <h3>Checkpoint — before moving on, you must be able to:</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Show a sub-60s one-take video demonstrating input → behavior → output</li>
            <li>Show a PPR with real code excerpts, matching the video</li>
            <li>Explain the PPR's exam-day role (WR2's only notes)</li>
            <li>Have both files backed up in two places</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <p>Need a deeper explanation? These pages cover the same concepts:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../exam/create-performance-task.html">Create PT guide</a> — video + PPR rules</li>
        <li><a href="../exam/written-responses.html">Written Responses</a> — how the PPR is used</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Next: <a href="11.2b.html">11.2b — Create PT: Submit as Final</a></p>
</div>`;
---
<Lesson id="11.2a" title="11.2a Create PT: Video + PPR — AP CS Principles" root=".." css="../style.css">
  <Fragment set:html={body} />
</Lesson>
